[00:00.00]Plip - one silver ripple starts to grow.
[00:10.58]Reef to shore,
[00:11.96]follow where the blue waves go.
[00:16.65]A is Angelfish,
[00:18.03]fins open wide |
[00:19.76]turning gently with the tide.
[00:22.18]B is Buoy, bobbing on blue |
[00:24.91]anchored while boats pass through.
[00:27.76]C is Coral, animals side by side |
[00:30.67]building reefs where fish hide.
[00:33.19]D is Dock,
[00:34.52]by the shore | boats tie up once more. E ... Eel!
[00:37.53]Long
[00:39.81]fish, no feet |
[00:41.32]bending through a rocky
[00:43.25]retreat.
[00:44.12]F is Fish, fins steer | gills take oxygen
[00:48.21]from water near. G ... Grouper!
[00:50.79]Waits by a ledge | broad mouth hiding near the edge.
[00:54.97]H is Harbor,
[00:56.18]sheltered from spray |
[00:57.68]calmer water where boats can stay.
[01:01.71]Ocean Letter Splash,
[01:04.06]come ride with me, Splash through letters,
[01:10.13]A to Z.
[01:12.72]Say the word,
[01:14.99]then feel the flow,
[01:18.14]Wave by
[01:19.72]wave,
[01:20.74]away
[01:21.50]we go.
[01:24.24]I? Island!
[01:25.64]Land ringed blue |
[01:27.61]water on every side, every view.
[01:30.47]J is Jetty,
[01:31.67]built from shore | guarding coasts or guiding channels. Kayak - that's
[01:36.46]K, paddle in hand |
[01:38.53]left then right,
[01:39.87]turn as planned.
[01:41.25]L ... Lobster!
[01:42.63]Walks the seafloor |
[01:44.08]long antennae
[01:45.20]feel what's before. M is Mussel,
[01:48.05]shell halves lock |
[01:49.50]silky threads hold tight to rock. N? Narwhal!
[01:53.11]Through Arctic blue |
[01:55.02]spiral tusk,
[01:56.28]one long tooth - true! O is Octopus,
[01:58.98]eight arms wide | soft body squeezes through to hide.
[02:03.19]P is Pelican, bill dips low | pouch catches fish, lets
[02:07.11]water flow.
[02:09.99]Ocean Letter Splash,
[02:12.33]come ride with me,
[02:15.35]Splash through letters,
[02:18.19]A to Z.
[02:20.86]Say the word,
[02:23.18]then feel
[02:24.20]the flow,
[02:26.36]Wave by
[02:27.78]wave, away
[02:29.64]we go. Q ...
[02:32.71]Quahog!
[02:34.06]Say KOH-hog | hard clam
[02:36.36]buried in sand or mud.
[02:38.61]R is Ray,
[02:39.89]fins spread wide |
[02:41.40]gliding low where shadows slide.
[02:43.80]S? Seahorse!
[02:45.34]Small and slow | curled tail grips seagrass
[02:48.07]in the flow.
[02:49.54]T is Turtle, at sea flippers sweep | steady through water
[02:53.39]deep.
[02:54.28]U ...
[02:55.02]Undersea Cave,
[02:56.28]dark below | seawater enters where sunlight can't go.
[03:00.47]V is Violet Sea Snail, afloat |
[03:03.67]hangs beneath its bubble raft. W is Whale, up for
[03:07.47]air | big breath,
[03:09.94]down from there.
[03:11.41]X? X-ray Tetra, freshwater
[03:13.67]not sea | translucent
[03:15.17]sides, some bones we see.
[03:18.74]Y is Yellowfin
[03:20.18]Tuna, finlets flash |
[03:22.17]streamlined body makes an ocean dash. Z ... Zooplankton!
[03:26.21]Ride the flow |
[03:27.80]tiny drifters where the currents go.
[03:31.71]Ocean Letter Splash,
[03:34.06]come ride with me, Splash through letters,
[03:40.13]A to Z.
[03:42.72]Say the word,
[03:45.04]then feel the flow,
[03:48.14]Wave by
[03:49.72]wave,
[03:50.85]away we go.
[03:54.47]My turn:
[03:56.72]I call the letter.
[03:59.04]You bring the word back. A ...
[04:01.82]Angelfish!
[04:03.11]Fan both hands and glide. B ... Buoy! Bob one hand
[04:05.36]with the
[04:09.33]tide.
[04:11.41]C ... Coral!
[04:12.70]Spread fingers
[04:13.98]side
[04:14.72]by side.
[04:16.83]D ... Dock! Make a platform
[04:19.82]by your side.
[04:21.45]E ... Eel!
[04:22.93]Wave one
[04:24.19]hand side
[04:25.57]to side.
[04:27.76]F ...
[04:28.56]Fish! Swish
[04:29.62]one hand
[04:30.98]and glide. G ...
[04:33.43]Grouper!
[04:34.42]Hide low
[04:35.78]by a ledge. H ... Harbor! Curve
[04:39.43]both hands
[04:40.67]into a bay.
[04:45.35]Ocean Letter Splash,
[04:47.76]come ride with me,
[04:50.80]Splash through letters,
[04:53.69]A to Z.
[04:56.28]Say the word,
[04:58.64]then feel the flow,
[05:01.78]Wave by
[05:03.37]wave,
[05:04.50]away we go. I ... Island! Circle one
[05:09.79]hand all around. J ... Jetty! Reach outward from solid ground.
[05:14.12]K ... Kayak! Paddle left, then right. L ... Lobster!
[05:18.07]Walk two fingers on the floor.
[05:21.45]M ... Mussel! Close two palms like a shell.
[05:24.97]N ... Narwhal! Trace one spiral tusk. O ... Octopus!
[05:28.64]Wiggle both hands, soft and slow. P ... Pelican! Scoop, then
[05:32.23]let the water go. Ocean Letter Splash, come
[05:39.99]ride with me,
[05:42.64]Splash through letters,
[05:45.55]A to Z.
[05:48.15]Say the word,
[05:50.47]then feel
[05:51.48]the flow,
[05:53.56]Wave by
[05:55.15]wave,
[05:56.17]away
[05:56.92]we go.
[06:00.36]Q ...
[06:01.90]Quahog!
[06:02.95]KOH-hog -
[06:05.11]close your clam. R ... Ray! Glide both hands
[06:09.94]above the sand.
[06:11.41]S ... Seahorse!
[06:12.88]Curl one finger in the flow.
[06:16.83]T ... Turtle! Sweep both hands
[06:19.82]as you go.
[06:21.47]U ...
[06:22.31]Undersea Cave!
[06:24.12]Arch both hands
[06:25.86]below.
[06:27.04]V ... Violet Sea Snail! Bubble-raft,
[06:30.66]float slow.
[06:32.47]W ...
[06:33.65]Whale!
[06:34.50]Rise for
[06:35.77]air,
[06:36.49]then dive. X ... X-ray Tetra!
[06:40.26]Freshwater
[06:41.01]fish -
[06:41.76]glide.
[06:46.02]Y ... Yellowfin
[06:47.39]Tuna! Sweep fast through the flow.
[06:52.10]Z ... Zooplankton!
[06:54.86]Drift where currents
[06:56.29]go.
[06:59.00]Ocean Letter Splash,
[07:01.35]come ride with me,
[07:04.36]Splash through letters,
[07:07.26]A to Z.
[07:10.09]Say the word,
[07:12.33]then feel the flow,
[07:15.43]Wave by
[07:17.01]wave,
[07:18.14]away we go.
[07:22.69]One last ripple
[07:24.12]reaches shore. A
[07:29.24]to Z,
[07:33.06]then
[07:33.85]one
[07:36.16]wave
[07:38.30]more.